  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan, respect the DBA‑only migration window, avoid touching the transactions table, handle the flaky notification check, and include compliance and architect sign‑offs. ZNB is more concrete: it specifies exact new columns, a feature‑flag rollout, a detailed rollback plan, and a clear 48‑hour deadline before the quarter, reducing ambiguity and likely fewer follow‑up questions. SMC is thorough but more abstract (e.g., “safe views/triggers”, separate acceptance‑criteria steps) and less explicit about rollout timing.",
